---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro';

const keys = [
  ['backend.url', 'Git repository URL of the personal sync repo'],
  ['security.encrypt_dotfiles', 'Encrypt dotfiles with AES-256-GCM. Default true'],
  ['security.scan_secrets', 'Scan team dotfiles for secrets. See Secret detection for the commands that scan. Default true'],
  ['dotfiles.files', 'Dotfiles to sync'],
  ['dotfiles.dirs', 'Folders to sync'],
  ['profiles.<name>.dotfiles', 'Dotfiles of a profile. An entry can be a table with path and on_conflict'],
  ['profiles.<name>.dirs', 'Folders of a profile'],
  ['profiles.<name>.packages', 'Package managers of a profile, such as ["brew", "npm"]. Empty means all enabled managers'],
  ['machine_profiles', 'The profile of each machine. Set it with tether machines profile set'],
  ['project_configs.enabled', 'Sync project configs, such as .env files'],
  ['project_configs.search_paths', 'Folders to search for projects'],
  ['project_configs.patterns', 'File patterns to sync in each project'],
  ['packages.<manager>.enabled', 'Sync this manager: brew, npm, pnpm, bun, gem or uv'],
  ['packages.min_release_age_days', 'Install only releases at least this many days old. Default 7. 0 turns it off. Homebrew has no limit'],
  ['packages.allow_scripts', 'npm, pnpm and bun packages that may run their install scripts'],
  ['packages.auto_install_from_trusted', 'Install packages from trusted machine records without a question. Default true'],
  ['packages.brew.trusted_taps', 'Homebrew taps outside homebrew/* that Tether may install from'],
  ['packages.brew.sync_casks', 'Sync Homebrew casks. Tether never installs casks on Linux'],
  ['packages.gem.auto_upgrade', 'Let the daemon upgrade gems, although a new dependency skips the release-age limit. Default false'],
  ['merge.command, merge.args', 'The merge tool for conflicts. See Conflicts'],
  ['dashboard.theme', 'Dashboard colors: auto, mocha, latte or ansi'],
];

const features = [
  ['personal_dotfiles', 'true', 'Sync personal dotfiles'],
  ['personal_packages', 'true', 'Sync personal package manifests'],
  ['collab_secrets', 'false', 'Share project secrets with GitHub collaborators'],
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Configuration — Tether CLI" description="Tether's config.toml keys, local.toml for one machine, and feature toggles.">
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE</p>
    <h1>Configuration</h1>
    <p>The configuration lives in <code>~/.tether/config.toml</code>. It syncs, encrypted, so all machines share it. A sync merges changes from two machines. See <a href="/docs/config-merge">Config merge</a>.</p>
    <Code code={`tether config get packages.min_release_age_days
tether config set packages.brew.trusted_taps '["oven-sh/bun"]'
tether config edit`} />
    <p><code>tether config set</code> reads the value as TOML, so arrays work. It refuses a key that the config does not have. The dashboard Config tab edits the same settings.</p>

    <h2>Example</h2>
    <Code lang="toml" label="~/.tether/config.toml" code={`[backend]
url = "git@github.com:you/dotfiles.git"

[security]
encrypt_dotfiles = true
scan_secrets = true

[dotfiles]
files = [".zshrc", ".gitconfig"]
dirs = [".config/nvim"]

[packages]
min_release_age_days = 7          # 0 turns the limit off
allow_scripts = ["esbuild"]       # packages that may run install scripts
auto_install_from_trusted = true  # false holds other machines' packages until you approve them

[packages.brew]
enabled = true
sync_casks = true
trusted_taps = ["oven-sh/bun"]    # taps outside homebrew/*

[packages.npm]
enabled = true`} />

    <h2>Keys</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{keys.map(([key, meaning]) => <tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td>{meaning}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Tether also writes keys that you do not edit: <code>config_version</code>, <code>config_writer</code>, and <code>sync_versions</code> for each manager, which 1.x builds need. A new config gets <code>sync_versions = false</code>, and an existing value stays.</p>

    <h2 id="local-config">Settings for one machine</h2>
    <p><code>~/.tether/local.toml</code> holds settings for this machine only. Tether never syncs it. Its values override <code>config.toml</code> on this machine. It takes these keys:</p>
    <Code lang="toml" label="~/.tether/local.toml" code={`[packages]
min_release_age_days = 14

[merge]
command = "vimdiff"
args = ["{local}", "{remote}", "{merged}"]   # the default when args is missing`} />

    <h2 id="feature-toggles">Feature toggles</h2>
    <Code code={`tether config features                   # list the toggles
tether config features enable <FEATURE>
tether config features disable <FEATURE>`} />
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Default</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{features.map(([name, def, meaning]) => <tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{def}</td><td>{meaning}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Example, team sync only:</p>
    <Code code={`tether config features disable personal_dotfiles
tether config features disable personal_packages`} />
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
